From 6f0b63889e7a967e96366b4ed9a53588e8805915 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (audit)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:06:22 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 03/14] students: tenant-safe homework/routines/schedules,
 personal copies for group homework

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011d4mgSxngjRmAXosGe4ry4

Security / data integrity
- Students could PATCH/DELETE their tutor's weekly routines and dated
  classes; writes are tutor-only now.
- Routines, dated classes and homework accepted any student/tuition id, so a
  tutor could attach rows to another tutor's group or student. Targets are
  checked against the tutor's own groups and manageable students.
- PATCH /homework/<id>/ with only a title always failed validation; partial
  updates now keep the existing target.
- A student's submission on shared group homework was written onto the row
  every classmate sees (and overwrote theirs). Submitting now creates the
  student's own copy (Homework.group_source); POST /homework/<id>/split/
  does the tutor's split atomically on the server.
- Homework file submissions go through the shared upload validator and the
  file URL is returned (submission_file_url) so tutors can open it.
- Student 'payment due' notifications no longer show the whole group's fee.
- Connected-tutor cards show a student only their own groups' routines.
- Invalid ?tutor_id no longer 500s.

Correctness / performance
- Tuition routine JSON is validated and normalised (day names, HH:MM).
- Tuition list/detail prefetch cycles and members (no N+1) and mutation
  responses are re-read so wallet figures are never stale.
- AttendanceCycle.ensure_active survives a creation race.
- Wallet totals and legacy cycle money use Decimal.
- Indexes for the hot filters; migration 0014 is additive only.
